Section 5, 'Puissances extérieures d'opérateurs de Fredholm, inégalités diverses', sets up a Fredholm-determinant calculus for trace-class (nuclear) operators u on a Hilbert space E. It uses normalized exterior products of operators.

Notation. u1∧…∧un is the symmetrized operator on the n-th exterior power, normalized with the factor 1/n!. Λ^n u (written \hat Λ_n u) is the operator induced on Λ^n E. α_n(u) is the n-th Fredholm coefficient, so det(1+zu) = Σ z^n α_n(u). ρ_i are the singular values (eigenvalues of |u|), and ||·||_1, ||·||_2 are the trace and Hilbert–Schmidt norms.

Prop. 1, (1): ||u1∧…∧un||_1 ≤ (1/n!) ||u1||_1 … ||un||_1.

Corollary 1. (2) The polarized Fredholm coefficient is a trace: α_n(u1,…,un) = Tr(u1∧…∧un). (3) In particular α_n(u) = Tr Λ^n u.

Corollary 2, (4): |α_n(u1,…,un)| ≤ (1/n!) ∏ ||ui||_1, and hence |α_n(u)| ≤ ||u||_1^n / n!.

Corollary 3, (5): |α_n(u)| ≤ α_n(|u|) = ||Λ^n u||_1 ≤ ||u||_1^n / n!. The proof uses three facts: |Tr| ≤ ||·||_1; Λ^n|u| = |Λ^n u|, so Tr Λ^n|u| = ||Λ^n u||_1; and (1). A crossed-out variant also records ||Λ^n u||_2 = sqrt(α_n(u*u)).

Corollary 4, (6): |det(1+u)| ≤ det(1+|u|). This follows by summing (5) over n.

Theorem 1. For u trace class:
- the eigenvalues satisfy (λ_i(u)) ∈ ℓ^1 (Weyl's inequality, proved on the previous page via exterior powers);
- (7) det(1+zu) = ∏(1+zλ_i(u));
- equivalently (8) α_n(u) = e_n(λ(u)), the n-th elementary symmetric function of the eigenvalues;
- (9) Tr u = Σ λ_i(u) is to be recovered from (8) by applying it to Λ^n u;
- (10) α_n(|u|) = ||Λ^n u||_1 = e_n(ρ(u)).
The text then claims: 'for the proof one reduces to the case u hermitian positive, where it is easy.'

Prop. 2, (11): ||(Λ^p u)∧(Λ^q v)||_1 ≤ [p!q!/(p+q)!] ||Λ^p u||_1 ||Λ^q v||_1 = [p!q!/(p+q)!] α_p(|u|) α_q(|v|). The note adds that the same holds for more than two factors, and that the notation (Λu)∧(Λv) is ambiguous here. The next page proves (11) from the Schmidt expansions of u and v.

Purpose. Prop. 2 feeds the next page:
- the binomial expansion Λ^m(u+v) = Σ binom(m,p) Λ^p u ∧ Λ^{m-p} v gives α_m(|u+v|) ≤ Σ_p α_p(|u|) α_{m-p}(|v|);
- hence det(1+r|u+v|) ≤ det(1+r|u|) det(1+r|v|);
- and the finite-m singular-value versions (15)–(17).
The whole page is groundwork for the Fredholm theory later published in 'La théorie de Fredholm' (Bull. SMF 1956) and the nuclear-operator material of Produits tensoriels topologiques.
